Z||000000||Heisenhund||06-01-2001||06:40 PM||||Hi all,<P>Planning on replacing my clutch in the next few days. I have 4 readily available brands to choose from and I was wondering if anyone had any input.<P>The contestants are: Borg-Warner, Cumberland, PowerTorque and a brand which is under the same company as the Zoom performance clutch.<P>Anybody have any experience with any of these guys?<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||06-01-2001||07:26 PM||||Not with any of these brands, but on my last Fiero (4spd) I used the Centerforce dual friction clutch.  Loved it!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kick.gif">  <BR>THE NORTHSTAR GIVES YOU A REAL KICK IN THE ASS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||06-01-2001||08:45 PM||||Borg Warner is the stock choice.<BR>Be sure that it is a new assembly. What prices are they in your area?||||reg||1
Z||000003||WMEBERT||06-01-2001||10:21 PM||||I can tell you by experience from working as a District Manager for AutoZone and now a Division Manager for Advance Auto parts that both companies buy their clutch's from Zoom. You'll get brand new Zoom parts from either company for a decent price with a lifetime warranty.  Check both stores-they'll price match each other.  (Buy from Advance-help my Bonus!!)  I've had one in my 86 GT for 2 years now with no problems.<P>Bill<BR>86 Fiero GT<BR>96 S10 4x4 Blazer<BR>2001 Ford Crown Vic.  V8, RWD!! (Company Car)  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Heisenhund||06-02-2001||08:30 AM||||I'm thinking Borg-Warner. I can get that for US$125 out the door.<P>And the clutches that AutoZone & Advance wanted to sell me were the Cumberland and the PowerTorque (respectively). Both the Borg & the Zoom are offered by Parks Auto.<P>Thanks all,<BR>Heis<BR>||||reg||1
